Title:          zfs.tcz
Description:    TESTING OpenZFS 2.4.4 userspace tools for CorePure64
Version:        2.4.4
Author:         OpenZFS project
Original-site:  https://github.com/openzfs/zfs
Copying-policy: CDDL-1.0
Size:           2M
Extension_by:   Zendrael
Tags:           zfs openzfs filesystem storage
Comments:       ----------
                OpenZFS 2.4.4 userspace for Tiny Core Linux CorePure64
                (x86_64). Kernel modules ship separately as
                zfs-modules-KERNEL.tcz (built for 6.18.35-tinycore64).
                Development files: zfs-dev.tcz.
                ----------
                Requires: CorePure64 with matching kernel modules
                (tce-load pulls zfs-modules-KERNEL.tcz).
                Not for 32-bit Core. Rebuild modules when TC bumps
                the kernel release.
                ----------
                CDDL note: OpenZFS is CDDL-1.0. Kernel modules are
                out-of-tree. Review license implications before
                redistributing with GPL-only policies.
                ----------
                Load:
                $ tce-load -i zfs.tcz
                ----------
                Load modules (after tce-load):
                $ sudo modprobe zfs
                ----------
                Import / mount pools:
                $ sudo zpool import -a
                $ sudo zfs mount -a
                Or use the init script:
                $ sudo /usr/local/etc/init.d/zfs start
                ----------
                Config: /usr/local/etc/zfs (symlinked as /etc/zfs)
                Optional helpers under /usr/local/lib/zfs/
                ----------
                This does NOT provide boot-from-ZFS / root-on-ZFS.
                Use for data pools after a normal CorePure64 boot.
                ----------
                This extension contains:
                openzfs-2.4.4 - CDDL-1.0 -
                https://github.com/openzfs/zfs/releases/tag/zfs-2.4.4
                ----------
